   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "霓虹疊塔 has no difficulty ramp after layer 35 — precise players never end",
   "detail": "speed = min(430, 150 + score·8) (index.html stack.tap) reaches its cap at layer 35 and nothing else changes; a perfect drop keeps the full width (perfect window max(3 px, 3%·w)) and 3 perfects in a row even widen it. World reached the 60-layer cap in 3/5 runs and superhuman in 2/3 (its one miss came from harness timing); skilled median 36, casual 19, clumsy 11.",
   "repro": "node qa/skill-tiers/vibe-arcade/bot.js world stack",
   "fix": "Keep ramping after 35 (e.g. speed = 150 + 8·min(score,35) + 3·max(0,score−35) with a higher cap, or shrink the perfect window / stop widening after N layers) so endless runs taper off."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "霓虹記憶: taps right after the last flash are silently dropped",
   "detail": "After the final flash goes dark the game stays in phase \"show\" for gap = max(0.08, 0.18−0.006·n) s before switching to \"input\"; press() ignores everything outside \"input\" (index.html simon.press / update). Probe: tapped the correct pad in that gap on round 1 → message stayed 「換你！ 0 / 1」, no feedback.",
   "repro": "Open 霓虹記憶, wait for the single flash to end and tap that pad within ~0.15 s.",
   "fix": "Switch to \"input\" as soon as the last light turns off (drop the trailing gap), or buffer taps made during the gap."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "閃電反應 floor is set by input latency, not by the player",
   "detail": "Superhuman (16 ms) scored 48–61 ms because the score is measured from the rAF frame time where the screen turned green to the pointerdown handler; ~35–45 ms of touch delivery is always included. Fine for humans (world 164–199 ms, casual 400–452, clumsy 525–776), but ratings (<200 ms 閃電之手) are reachable only by top players; tiers separate cleanly.",
   "repro": "node qa/skill-tiers/vibe-arcade/bot.js superhuman react",
   "fix": "Optional: use e.timeStamp of the pointer event instead of performance.now() in react.tap to remove part of the handler delay."
  },
